# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal, never published
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Product documentation, the decision register and the working notes stay on
# the owner's disk. A fresh clone therefore carries no project context, which
# is a known and accepted consequence.
docs/
CLAUDE.md

# Internal tooling. Scripts we use ourselves and never ship. Backed up outside
# this repository.
tools/

# The developer changelog became internal on 2026-08-02. It was tracked until
# then, so the history up to that day stays in this repository and only future
# edits are untracked, exactly as with the documents above.
#
# It keeps the writing conventions of the repository even though it has left
# it, English and the punctuation rules included, because sentences move
# between it and the public changelog next to it. That exception is named in
# tools/audyt.py rather than left to memory.
CHANGELOG-DEV.md

# Local assistant configuration. Machine specific and not part of the product.
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated datasets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project is a data generator, so its own working directory fills with
# output faster than any other repository would. These are anchored to the
# root on purpose, so that a package called data or output somewhere inside
# the source tree is still tracked.
/data/
/out/
/output/
/fixtures/

# Loose manifests dropped by a run at the root. Manifests inside testdata are
# committed on purpose, because they are fixtures.
/manifest.json
/manifest.csv
/manifest.md
/manifest.gherkin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/qadg
/qadg.exe
/qadg-gui
/qadg-gui.exe
/bin/
/dist/
/build/

# Compiled objects, including anything cgo leaves behind when the GUI module
# is built.
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.syso

# Test binaries and coverage. Named exactly rather than by extension, because
# a pattern like *.out would also swallow golden files under testdata.
*.test
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.coverprofile

# Profiling output
*.prof
*.pprof
cpu.pprof
mem.pprof
trace.out

# Go workspace files. Useful locally when both modules are edited together and
# meaningless to anybody else.
go.work
go.work.sum

# We do not vendor dependencies, so a vendor directory means somebody was
# experimenting.
/vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GUI packaging
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fyne packaging output and the cross build helper.
/fyne-cross/
*.app/
*.dmg
*.msi
*.rpm
*.deb

# The compatibility package ships a software OpenGL implementation next to the
# binary. That is build output, not source.
opengl32.dll
libgallium_wgl.dll

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.local
.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Output of the internal tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backups left behind by a mutation run that was interrupted. The next run
# finds them and puts the original files back, so they are recovered rather
# than deleted, and they are never committed.
#
# The suffix is not English because it is not a name given here. The file is
# written by tools/mutacje.py, which lives outside this repository on the
# Polish side of the language rule, so this pattern has to match the name that
# script actually writes. Translating it would stop it matching anything.
*.mutacja-bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, so that nobody adds them later by reflex
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# testdata/     Go treats it as committed fixture data and the determinism
#               golden files live there. Ignoring it would silently disable
#               the test that protects the most important invariant.
# go.sum        Required for reproducible builds.
# spec/         Public specifications. The whole point of the repository.
